# Renders.
#
# Both bin/glitchvape and bin/glitchvape-batch default their output here, so
# this fills with megabytes on the first run and with hundreds of megabytes
# after an afternoon of --all-presets. Nothing in it is source: every file is
# reproducible from its seed and the settings that produced it.
#
# Unanchored, so a batch run started from a subdirectory is caught too.
out/

# Source photographs.
#
# The input side of the same coin, and not the program's to distribute.
Pictures/

# Typefaces.
#
# A font belongs in this repository only if what it is licensed under is
# written down beside it. That is the rule `make check-licenses` applies, and
# it is structural rather than a list to keep up to date: a release unpacked
# whole -- LICENSE, README and all -- may be committed; a font file dropped in
# loose may not, because nothing beside it says what its terms are.
#
# Being in the repository and being in the packages are two different
# questions, and they are answered by two different directories:
#
#   assets/fonts/           free to redistribute. Ships in the base package.
#   assets/fonts-nonfree/   documented but restricted. Ships in
#                           glitchvape-fonts-extra, and nowhere else.
#
# The split is what lets the base package state one honest licence -- MIT AND
# OFL-1.1 -- and mean it, while a font whose terms are narrower than that is
# still in the tree, still found in a checkout, and still installable by
# anybody who wants it.
#
# Restricted today: only W95FA, which arrived from a font aggregator without
# the licence it is said to be under -- a claim about the terms rather than
# the terms. Nothing breaks without it: GlitchVape::Fonts falls through each
# role's candidate list to whatever fontconfig can see, and --check-fonts
# names the download and the directory to put it in. See "Fonts" in the
# README.
#
# VCR OSD Mono used to be held back too. Its author has since answered the
# question directly -- free for any purpose, commercial included -- so it is
# an ordinary bundled font now, and its LICENSE records where he said so.
#
# Everything under both directories is ignored by default and the releases
# that are ours to hand on are named back in, one line each. Adding a font is
# therefore a deliberate line here plus the licence beside it, and never
# something that happens by forgetting.
assets/fonts/*
!assets/fonts/DepartureMono-1.500/
!assets/fonts/fusion-pixel-font-12px-monospaced-otf-v2026.08.11/
!assets/fonts/VCROSD/

assets/fonts-nonfree/*
!assets/fonts-nonfree/W95FA/

# Artwork is deliberately NOT ignored: assets/artwork/logo.png is a few
# kilobytes, is this project's own, and the about window needs it.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output

# Generated from the tools' own POD at install time -- see `make man` -- so
# that a page can never disagree with the --help of the tool it documents.
# Nothing here is edited by hand.
/glitchvape.1
/glitchvape-batch.1
/glitchvape-gui.1

# The source tarball and the tree it is built from.
/glitchvape-[0-9]*.tar.gz
/glitchvape-[0-9]*/

# What dpkg-buildpackage leaves inside debian/. The .deb files themselves
# land in the parent directory, which is outside this repository.
debian/files
debian/tmp/
debian/.debhelper/
debian/*.substvars
debian/*.debhelper.log
debian/debhelper-build-stamp
debian/glitchvape/
debian/glitchvape-gui/
debian/glitchvape-fonts-extra/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated by the tools this project is checked with

# perltidy leaves a .bak when it is run without the -bext='/' that the
# Makefile-less workflow in the README uses, writes a .ERR beside any file it
# could not parse, and a .LOG when asked for one.
*.bak
*.ERR
*.LOG
*.tdy

# prove --state
.prove

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local tooling and editors

# Claude Code keeps shared settings in .claude/settings.json and personal ones
# -- permission grants, machine-specific paths -- in the .local.json beside
# it. Only the personal half is ignored, so a shared config can still be
# committed if there is ever a reason to.
.claude/settings.local.json

.vscode/
.idea/

*~
*.swp
*.swo

.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
